  "id": "stroboscope",
  "term": "stroboscope",
  "definition": "A stroboscope is a device that creates the appearance of continuous movement by letting the viewer see a rapid series of slightly different pictures in brief glimpses, usually through slits in a rotating card or cylinder. Historical forms include the phenakistoscope and zoetrope.",
